  "tagline": "Mass-manufactured nuclear power plants, purpose-built to power AI data centers",
  "description": "Aalo Atomics is an Austin-based nuclear energy company that mass-manufactures sodium-cooled modular reactors built to power AI data centers. Founded in 2023 by Matt Loszak and Yasir Arafat, it builds the 10 MWe Aalo-1 reactor and the 50 MWe Aalo Pod, designed to be truck-transportable and factory-built for sub-year deployment at data-centre sites. Aalo achieved first criticality of its Aalo-X test reactor at Idaho National Laboratory on July 4, 2026 and has raised more than $130 million across three disclosed rounds, including a $100 million Series B led by Valor Equity Partners.",
